import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'own-open-door':('The Borg stands in an open doorway','A Warrior with a burned-out torch stands in an open doorway whose grid the game reports as lit, while the Borg\'s own map carries no glow mark for it (the state the door case exists to repair). The original scan visits only the eight neighbours, so the own-grid door case never fires and the lit mark is never repaired; the corrected scan includes the Borg\'s own grid, the door case fires, and the mark is set.'),
 'floor':('Control: the own grid is a plain lit floor','With a plain lit floor underfoot both versions leave the marks alone. The complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/calllight-231 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP ownfeat=','setup'),('STATE ','state'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The call-light scan never visited the Borg's own grid</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native call-light scans</p><h1>The call-light scan never visited the Borg's own grid</h1><p>The out-of-light routine's call-light scan loops over the eight neighbouring grids, but one branch inside it tests the Borg's own grid — the case for standing in an open doorway whose lit state the Borg's map lacks. That case could never fire, and the cheat that reads the truth from the game (is the doorway grid lit?) never ran. The correction includes index 8 of the direction table, the Borg's own grid.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The doorway</button><button data-step="1">After the scan</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With a plain lit floor underfoot both versions leave the marks alone and the logs match byte for byte, so the correction changes only the own-grid doorway case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, depth 30, seed 1000, glowing constructed arena (the game's doorway grid is lit), a burned-out torch putting the routine into its out-of-light path, spare torches and the recall scroll removed from the pack (recorded fixture intervention) so the wear-stuff, refuel and recall branches have nothing to act on first. The Borg's own grid is planted without a glow mark — the state the door case repairs. The production routine runs directly; the tracked mark is read back, nothing is cast.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/231">issue231</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function markLabel(c){if(!c||!c.state)return'?';return c.state.ownglow?'Own grid marked glowing':'Own grid left unmarked'}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Own grid feat ${d.setup?d.setup.ownfeat:'?'}, game says lit.`:markLabel(d);p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The doorway grid is lit; the Borg\\'s map lacks the mark.':'The scan either repairs the mark or leaves it.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?markLabel(d):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='own-open-door'?'The original leaves the doorway unmarked; the correction repairs it from the game.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
